.Dd July 3, 2026
.Dt XTC_IOSCHED 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xtc_iosched_create ,
.Nm xtc_iosched_destroy ,
.Nm xtc_iosched_write ,
.Nm xtc_iosched_flush ,
.Nm xtc_iosched_get_stats
.Nd adaptive write-batching scheduler for the async file path
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xtc.h
.In xtc_iosched.h
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_iosched_create "const xtc_iosched_opts_t *opts" "xtc_iosched_t **out"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_iosched_destroy "xtc_iosched_t *s"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_iosched_write "xtc_iosched_t *s" "const void *buf" "uint32_t len" "int64_t off"
.Ft int
.Fn xtc_iosched_flush "xtc_iosched_t *s"
.Ft void
.Fn xtc_iosched_get_stats "const xtc_iosched_t *s" "xtc_iosched_stats_t *out"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm xtc_iosched
is an adaptive write-batching scheduler for a single writer over the
async file path
.Pq Xr xtc_aio 3 ,
intended for the direct-I/O writeback hot path such as a buffer
manager flusher or a WAL writer.  Queued writes are coalesced into
batches; each flush issues the batch via
.Fn xtc_aio_pwrite
and measures throughput.  When adaptive mode is enabled a genetic
tuner
.Pq Xr xtc_dio_sched 3
evolves the batch size to maximise observed throughput and re-adapts
when the workload or device behaviour shifts; with adaptive off it
uses a fixed batch size.
.Pp
.Sy Single-writer contract :
all calls for one scheduler must come from one fiber (the device's
writer).  This keeps batching free of cross-fiber coordination;
flushing parks only that fiber.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_iosched_create
creates a scheduler from
.Fa opts :
the target descriptor
.Fa fd ,
whether to
.Fa adaptive Ns -tune
the batch size, the fixed or initial
.Fa batch_size ,
the
.Fa min_batch Ns / Ns Fa max_batch
gene bounds when adaptive, and the tuner PRNG
.Fa seed .
.Pp
.Fn xtc_iosched_write
queues a
.Fa len Ns -byte
write of
.Fa buf
at offset
.Fa off .
The buffer must remain valid until the next flush completes.  When the
queue reaches the current batch size an implicit flush runs, issuing
the batch and possibly parking the writer fiber.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_iosched_flush
issues all queued writes immediately.
.Pp
.Fn xtc_iosched_get_stats
copies the scheduler's counters into
.Fa out :
total
.Fa writes
queued,
.Fa bytes
written,
.Fa flushes
issued, the
.Fa cur_batch
size in use, the
.Fa last_mbps
throughput of the last flush, and the tuner
.Fa mutation_rate
(adaptive only).
.Pp
.Fn xtc_iosched_destroy
frees the scheduler.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn xtc_iosched_create ,
.Fn xtc_iosched_write ,
and
.Fn xtc_iosched_flush
return
.Dv XTC_OK
on success or a negative errno / 
.Dv XTC_E_*
code from the underlying flush.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xtc_aio 3 ,
.Xr xtc_dio_sched 3 ,
.Xr xtc_fs 3
.Sh AUTHORS
.An The XTC Project .
